  "entry": "code/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A Streamlit app for research and training use. A chemist loads a sample-by-feature table, picks a preprocessing method and explores it with PCA. They flag outlier samples with Hotelling's T² and Q-residual limits, fit a cross-validated PLS regression to a numeric target, and check feature influence, applicability domain and uncertainty before exporting CSVs and the fitted model. Data used in the run: synthetic. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
